Title: seat-runner self-test needlessly injects the endpoint credential
Created: 2026-07-14
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-07-14T13:40Z claude created
2026-07-14T22:02Z claude note planned by raid — --no-cred flag param; argv is the only discriminating test channel (env-dump is tautological)

--- body ---
## Context

Follow-up to tickets/0207-agnostic-cli-reviewer-seat-one-config-op.erg, raised
by the review-pr red-team panel on PR #603 (0207 criterion-2 credential
scrub). `run_seat` always passes `CRED_ARGS` — including a real injected
`OPENAI_API_KEY` — into the pre-review containment self-test container, not only
the actual reviewer run. The self-test never needs the endpoint credential: it
only probes write/secret/network containment. This is a latent least-privilege
gap. It is currently a non-issue in practice because the self-test runs under
`--network=none` with no relay and cannot exfiltrate, and its probe output
(`$PROBE`) is asserted line-by-line rather than echoed wholesale — but the key
should not be in that container's env at all, and `$PROBE` is not run through
the 0207 scrub.

## Relevant files
- `scripts/seat-runner.sh` — `run_seat` (CRED_ARGS injection), the containment
  self-test call (`PROBE=$(run_seat bash -c '…')`), and the scrub chokepoint.

## Actions
1. Give `run_seat` a way to omit `CRED_ARGS` (e.g. a flag or a variant) so the
   self-test container runs with only the dummy key, never the real one.
2. Confirm no self-test assertion depends on the real key; the probe only needs
   the dummy.

## Test
- Extend `tests/test_seat_runner.sh`: with `--credential-env` set to a probe
  value, assert the SELF-TEST podman invocation's captured env does NOT contain
  the real value (only the review run may), mirroring the existing argv/env
  capture stubs.

## Invariants
- The review run still receives the real credential; the scrub still covers all
  three reviewer-output echo paths.
- `make check-fast` and `tests/test_seat_runner.sh` stay green.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The containment self-test container never receives the real endpoint key.
- [ ] A test proves the self-test env carries only the dummy key.
